# .env.example -- documentation only. It contains NO real values and must never gain any.
#
# The StudyAI frontend reads no environment variables: it is a static, local-first app, and nothing in src/
# uses import.meta.env. There is therefore nothing to copy from this file, and no `.env` file is needed.
#
# Real secrets live ONLY in:
#   * Cloudflare secrets (set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`), for the deployed Worker, and
#   * `.dev.vars` (untracked, ignored by git), for local Worker development. See `.dev.vars.example`.
#
# Never put a secret in a VITE_* variable: Vite inlines those into the public JavaScript bundle.
# `.env` and `.env.*` are git-ignored, and `pnpm scan:secrets` fails if one is ever tracked or found in history.
